<<~ ahu slot=`#/body`>>

Carry-Wright: Lares (Tasked Spirit). Read CLAUDE.md once for house law, then implement. This is an IMPLEMENTATION task: start editing code within your first few actions. Do not write a plan file, do not stop at a trace. Done means the diff below exists and the listed tests pass.

CONTEXT (all measured; no need to re-trace):
* `packages/lararium-tw5/src/action-handler.ts` now refuses an INGEST whose `sourceUri` does not rest under the destination bag's granted mirror root (`assertDiskWavePlacement`, `DiskWavePlacementRefusal`, code `disk-wave-placement`).
* `lares import` (`packages/lares-cli/src/commands/carry.ts`) ingests each wave straight from the bundle directory: the `wave(...)` helper (~line 538) calls `doors.ingest({ source: sourceDir, ... })`, and `LIVE_CARRY_DOORS.ingest` (~line 141) calls `settleIngest({ source: wave.source, ... })`. Under the new ward every such wave refuses.
* The export side already knows each wave's mirror directory (`mirrorDir`, passed to `wave(...)`, used by `mirrorDirFileToUri`).

CHANGE (make exactly this):
# In `carry.ts`'s `wave(...)`, when `apply` is true and there are candidates or kāpae: copy each wave file from the bundle (`join(bundle.root, ...)`) into `mirrorDir` at the same relative path BEFORE calling `doors.ingest`, then pass `source: mirrorDir` (not `sourceDir`) to `doors.ingest`.
#* Write a file only when it is absent at the destination, or present with byte-identical content. If a different file already stands there, do NOT overwrite: record it in `workTally.stoodOff` as `"<uri> (a different file stands in the mirror; left as it stands)"` and leave it out of the candidates.
#* Write through the existing atomic writer if the CLI has one (grep `atomicWrite` / `writeFileAtomic` in packages/lares-cli/src and packages/lararium-node/src); create parent dirs; mode 0600 for files.
#* `.kapae` shadow files copy the same way (they ride in `scan.shadows`).
# Keep `LIVE_CARRY_DOORS.ingest` as is apart from receiving the mirror source.
# Update the module comment of the wave helper to say: an import restores each file into its mirror, then the ingest reads it from there, so the placement ward reads a source under the bag's own mirror.

TESTS (red first, in `packages/lares-cli/tests/carry-verbs.test.ts`, using its existing fake doors and scratch root):
a. An apply import copies a wave's files into the mirror dir and calls ingest with `source` equal to that mirror dir.
b. A mirror file that already holds different bytes stays untouched, lands in stoodOff, and is not a candidate.
c. A re-run import (journal) writes nothing new and calls ingest with no repeated candidates.
Then run: `cd packages/lares-cli && npx vitest run tests/carry-verbs.test.ts --maxWorkers=4`, then the full lares-cli suite with `--maxWorkers=4`; <code>pnpm &#45;-filter &#64;lares/cli build &amp;&amp; node tools/stamp-build.mjs . &#45;-pkg lares-cli</code>; <code>pnpm &#45;-filter &#64;lares/cli typecheck</code>; `node tools/evergreen-boundary.mjs`.

LIMITS: edit only packages/lares-cli/src/commands/carry*.ts and packages/lares-cli/tests/carry-verbs.test.ts (plus a tiny shared helper in lares-cli if truly needed). No git commit, no push, no stash. Never touch ~/.lares or docker. If a test outside these files fails for reasons unrelated to your change, note it and continue.

FINAL MESSAGE: the files changed, each test's result with counts, and anything you could not do.

